this is a docker file for apache:

start docker file..

~ FROM ubuntu:latest
~ 
~ MAINTAINER p4r54-apache
~ 
~ RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y apache2 && apt-get clean && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*
~ 
~ ENV APACHE_RUN_USER=www-data
~ ENV APACHE_RUN_GROUP=www-data
~ ENV APACHE_LOG_DIR=/var/log/apache2
~ 
~ EXPOSE 80
~ 
~ CMD ["/usr/sbin/apache2", "-D", "FOREGROUND"]

..end of docker-file

note: save the file by name of "Dockerfile"
note: RUN arguments are run inside of the pulled ubuntu container
note: EXPOSE indicates that the container is listening on port 80 (and doesnt relate to host machine you will specify that later)

the procedure will be like:
Docker-file <--(build)--> docker image <--(run)--> container

steps:

-enter the directory of your docker file.
-build docker-file:
	>>> docker build -t apache-image-name ./
you specify the name of your image and location of the docker-file

	>>> docker images
apache-image-name image is created

run the image to container:
	>>> docker run -p 8000:80 --name=apache_container1 apache-image-name
check the browser to see apache

in another terminal see the container running:
	>>> docker ps

stop the container:
	>>> docker stop container_ID

